# Seals reference these files by CONTENT HASH (SPEC 3.3), so a single byte
# matters. On Windows, Git would otherwise rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout —
# one extra byte per line, a different SHA-256, and every seal referencing the
# dictionary becomes unresolvable, silently.
#
# Same reasoning for the test vectors and the pilot: their hashes are published.
docs/profiles/*.json  -text
test-vectors/*.json   -text
test-vectors/*.pubkey -text
pilot/*               -text
*.json                text eol=lf
